  "question": {
    "text": "The solution of the differential equation\r\n\r\n$(x+1) \\frac{d y}{d x}-y=e^{3 x}(x+1)^{2}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "o491H",
      "text": "$y=(x+1) e^{3 x}+c$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wF9eq",
      "text": "$3 y=(x+1)+e^{3 x}+c$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "V8ZAY",
      "text": "$\\frac{3 y}{x+1}=e^{3 x}+c$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "o5TXK",
      "text": "$y e^{-3 x}=3(x+1)+c$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The given equation is $\\frac{d y}{d x}-\\frac{y}{x+1}=e^{3 x}(x+1)$\r\n\r\nI.F. $=e^{\\int-\\frac{1}{x+1} d x}=e^{-\\log (x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x+1}$\r\n\r\nThe solution is\r\n\r\n$y\\left(\\frac{1}{x+1}\\right)=\\int e^{3 x}(x+1) \\cdot \\frac{1}{x+1} d x+a$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{y}{x+1}=\\int e^{3 x} d x+a=\\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}+a$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{3 y}{x+1}=e^{3 x}+c, c=3 a$",
    "image": null
  },
